# TODO - Jig repository governance

## Objective

Integrate the evolving Jig validator as repository-local tooling, preserve its
fail-closed rules, and configure only genuine project-specific differences
without weakening unrelated linter contracts.

## Acceptance

- The repository-local Jig installation and `jig.toml` describe the actual
  polyglot repository without fake language/tool requirements or weakened
  reviewed lint policy.
- The authoritative rule/specification is deterministic, versionable, and does
  not depend on undocumented host behavior.
- The declared scope contains no unresolved placeholder implementation or
  undocumented workaround required for this objective to function.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.

## Evidence

- Repository-local Jig 26.3.1 remains installed through the source-linked
  launcher under `.dependencies/jig/bin/`; the active development authority now
  requires configuration schema 8.
- `jig.toml` schema 8 declares the repository-owned typed TODO workflow: task
  document, open/completed roots, record extension, exact sections, acceptance
  evidence, validation commands, and strict dependency-lane ordering. It also
  declares closed change-class path policy for architecture, implementation,
  bugfix, tests, documentation, and dependency admission.
- The installed commit-message hook parses the schema-8 configuration and accepts
  new compliant commits fail-closed.
- Full `jig validate --root .` remains fail-closed. The source-linked Jig moved
  from schema 7 to schema 8 during this migration; Malbolge follows the published
  configuration contract without bypassing its hook or editing that concurrent
  tool worktree.
- Completion remains blocked until the current source-linked Jig and the complete
  repository validate cleanly under the same authority.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `repository-responsibility-scaffold`.
